  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened social protection and improved labour administration, enhancing wage system and  workplace compliance policies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Samoa has prioritised the improvement of labour administration, improving minimum wage, eradicating child street vendors and social protection as key areas for development in this biennium. The ILO continues to support the strengthening and implementation of social protection systems to safeguard workers&#x2019; rights and wellbeing. This includes initiatives aimed at increasing minimum wage, maternity protection and other social protection. In this regard, ILO also provides technical support to ensure adequate social protection measures are in place through the legislative and policy amendments adopted for implementation of C190 and C187 including Labour and Employment Relations Amendment Act 2023 as well as OSH policy and legislative review. ILO also provides technical support towards the establishment of a monitoring and evaluation framework to track and assess adherence to social protection guidelines and regulations. In addition, ILO provides technical and financial support towards the implementation of Roadmap priorities under the Alliance 8.7 work plan on the elimination of child street vendors. This is through enhancing legal and policy frameworks, enhancing community engagement with vulnerable families and cultural entertainment initiatives aimed at removing the street vendors from the street and training them in the fire knife dancing skills while encouraging them to complete formal education.</narrative>
  </description>
